1
00:00:00,426 --> 00:00:02,516
(Amy:)Read about it in your book.

2
00:00:04,063 --> 00:00:05,993
(Bernadette:)Why would you be embarrassed
to tell us?

3
00:00:06,165 --> 00:00:09,465
I'm not. I didn't want anyone to know.
I haven't told Leonard yet.

4
00:00:09,668 --> 00:00:12,898
- Why wouldn't you tell Leonard?
- Because it's me going back to school.

5
00:00:13,072 --> 00:00:15,902
(Penny:)And he's gonna be all,
"You can do it," and, "How can I help?"

6
00:00:16,075 --> 00:00:18,545
And, "I'm so proud of you." Ugh.

7
00:00:20,179 --> 00:00:23,079
I can't believe you could keep
something like that from him.

8
00:00:23,249 --> 00:00:26,049
(Amy:)You guys have got to be
the weirdest couple I know.

9
00:00:32,591 --> 00:00:34,921
(Penny:)Really?

10
00:00:35,628 --> 00:00:38,258
(Penny:)You can't think of anyone weirder?

11
00:00:40,199 --> 00:00:41,219
(Amy:)I can...

12
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,830
(Amy:)...but she's sitting right there.

13
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:50,870
Yes. I play the word "quiver"...

14
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:56,100
(Sheldon:)...with a triple letter
and a double word score for 72 points.

15
00:00:56,682 --> 00:01:01,022
That'll let the air out of your tires,
Hawking.

